{\*\ftnsep\chftnsep}\pgndec\pard\plain \s1\keep\sb360\sa80\keepn\cf18\rtlch\af8\afs40\ltrch\hich\af5\afs40\dbch\af8\loch\f5\fs40\keep\sb360\sa80\keepn{
{\*\bkmkstart intelligent-page-breaks}Intelligent page breaks}
\par \pard\plain \s89{
While there is no direct support in Excel for Widow/Orphan control, FlexCel has the capacity to add page breaks to your file, so you can keep interesting sections together.}
\par \pard\plain \s85\sb180\sa180{\rtlch\ab\ltrch\b
Make sure to read the conceptual documentation about }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://doc.tmssoftware.com/flexcel/vcl/guides/api-developer-guide.html#intelligent-page-breaks" }{\fldrslt {\cf20\rtlch\ab\ltrch\b
Intelligent Page Breaks}{}}}\rtlch\ab\ltrch\b
 to better understand what we are doing here.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\keep\sb160\sa80\keepn\cf18\rtlch\af8\afs32\ltrch\hich\af5\afs32\dbch\af8\loch\f5\fs32{
{\*\bkmkstart concepts}Concepts}
\par \pard\plain \s0\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\kerning0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1025\ltrch\hich\af4\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720{
How to add automatic page breaks to a sheet. In this case, we are dumping a Pascal file to PDF, and we want to keep procedures in the same page is possible.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\kerning0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1025\ltrch\hich\af4\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720{
How to deal with different levels of "keep together". FlexCel allows you to make some rows more "keep together" than others, if it can't fit everything in the same page, it will try to keep the rows of higher "keep together". We use this here to try to keep full classes first, if it is not possible full procedures, if not full for/while loops, etc.\line Each }{\rtlch\ab\ltrch\b
begin}{
 sign in the source file means higher level of "keep together", and each }{\rtlch\ab\ltrch\b
end}{
 decreases the level.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\kerning0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1025\ltrch\hich\af4\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720\sb0\sa200{
The method }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://doc.tmssoftware.com/flexcel/vcl/api/FlexCel.Core/TExcelFile/AutoPageBreaks.html" }{\fldrslt {\cf20
TExcelFile.AutoPageBreaks}{}}}
 must be called after everything is done, so the sheet is in a final state when applying the page breaks.{\*\bkmkend intelligent-page-breaks}{\*\bkmkend concepts}}
\par }